# Build context for the AGENT image (deploy-agent.sh runs `--source agent`).
#
# This one matters more than it looks. The Dockerfile here does:
#
#     COPY . .
#
# which is convenient and takes whatever happens to be sitting in this folder.
# By the time you deploy, `adk web` has been running here for two hours and has
# left rehearsal state behind. None of it should reach a container.

# --- state adk web leaves behind -----------------------------------------
# sessions.db is the one to think about. SESSION_SERVICE_URI points at Cloud SQL
# in production, so a stale file would normally be ignored -- but it only takes
# one deploy with the variable unset for the container to quietly use a database
# full of somebody's rehearsal instead, and nothing about that looks broken.
sessions.db
sessions-*.db
nightly.db
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
artifacts/
.adk/

# memory/ is a local fallback. In production MEMORY_DIR is a gs:// bucket, so a
# file baked in here is a second source of truth waiting to disagree with it.
memory/

# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# If .env is ever copied in here it holds the Cloud SQL password. Image layers
# are readable by anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# --- python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# --- editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- assistant tooling ---------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.claude*/
CLAUDE.md
.antigravity/
.antigravity*/
.cursor/
.aider*
AGENTS.md
.agent/
